Subject: [PATCH] MIRAGE: unlink, link, truncate, install, shred; and cat as
 cat is

Five commands that change files were left to the responder's model, which
describes a change as a list of operations and described the wrong one
about one time in four while reporting success (a directory for
truncate, nothing for install): the session was told a file was made and
then shown that it was not. A command whose effect is a function of its
arguments and the tree is the emulator's. Each implements the common
options and declines the rest.

cat ended every file with a newline whether it had one or not (printf
abc > f; cat f | wc -c said 4), accepted -A -b -e -E -s -t -T -v and did
nothing for them, numbered lines with two spaces where cat puts a tab,
and read any file for any user. It is coreutils 9.1's now, and a file the
user may not read is refused.

All held to recordings of the reference host: 81 command lines added to
test/mirage_file_reference.jsonl.
